       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because of amlodipine's long half-life, toxicity can last a long time. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nCould this be a typo or a unit error? Here are some options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily:** the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily:** the maximum dose.\n- **Another regimen:** if you meant a different drug or a split regimen, tell me.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note that you've confirmed it is intentional. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
